
Testing the ArrayList
==================================================

Test case 1 [ArrayList]: add methods: add(E), add(int,E), addFirst(E), addLast(E)
list: [44 11 33 66 22 88 55 77]

Test case 2 [ArrayList]: clone method
[44 11 33 66 22 88 55 77].clone() = [44 11 33 66 22 88 55 77]

Test case 3 [ArrayList]: Collection methods: addAll, containsAll, retainAll, removeAll
[111 77 222 55].addAll([44 11 33 66 22 88 55 77]) = [111 77 222 55 44 11 33 66 22 88 55 77]
[44 11 33 66 22 88 55 77].retainAll([111 77 222 55]) = [55 77]
[44 11 33 66 22 88 55 77].removeAll([111 77 222 55]) = [44 11 33 66 22 88]
[44 11 33 66 22 88 55 77].containsAll([44 11 33 66 22 88 55 77]) = true
[11 33 66 22 88 55 77].containsAll([44 11 33 66 22 88 55 77]) = false

Test case 4 [ArrayList]: (getters) get(int), getFirst(), getLast()
[11 33 66 22 88 55 77]
[11 33 66 22 88 55 77].get(3) = 22
[11 33 66 22 88 55 77].getFirst() = 11
[11 33 66 22 88 55 77].getLast() = 77

Test case 5 [ArrayList]: set method
[11 33 66 22 88 55 77].set(3, 44) = 22
Modified list : [11 33 66 44 88 55 77]

Test case 6 [ArrayList]: (remove methods) remove(Object), remove(int), removeFirst(), removeLast()
list: [44 11 33 66 22 88 55 77]
remove(55) = true
removeFirst() = 44
removeLast() = 77
remove(2) = 66
Modified list: [11 33 22 88]

Test case 7 [ArrayList]: (search methods) contains(Object), indexOf(Object), lastIndexOf(Object)
[11 33 66 44 88 55 77].contains(88) = true
[11 33 66 44 88 55 77].contains(111) = false
[11 33 66 44 88 55 77].indexOf(55) = 5
[11 33 66 44 88 55 77].indexOf(222) = -1
[11 33 66 44 88 55 77].lastIndexOf(77) = 6
[11 33 66 44 88 55 77].lastIndexOf(222) = -1
Unmodified list: [11 33 66 44 88 55 77]

Test case 8 [ArrayList]: (iterator methods) iterator, listIterator, listIterator(int)
list: [11 33 66 44 88 55 77]
Iterator from 0 to 6: 11 33 66 44 88 55 77 
ListIterator from 0 to 6, then from 6 to 0: 11 33 66 44 88 55 77 77 55 88 44 66 33 11 
ListIterator from 3 to 0, then from 0 to 6: 44 66 33 11 11 33 66 44 88 55 77 

Test case 9 [ArrayList]: equals method
[11 33 66 44 88 55 77].equals([111 77 222 55]) ? false
[11 33 66 44 88 55 77].equals([11 33 66 44 88 55 77]) ? true

Test case 10 [ArrayList]: sort method
list: [11 33 66 44 88 55 77]
list sorted using the natural ordering: [11 33 44 55 66 77 88]

list: [1000 900 1500 33 555 88]
list sorted using the number of digits (ties: descending value): [88 33 900 555 1500 1000]

Test case 11 [ArrayList]: toArray method
[11 33 44 55 66 77 88].toArray() = [11 33 44 55 66 77 88 ]

Test case 12 [ArrayList]: reversed method
list: [88 33 900 555 1500 1000]
reversed list: [1000 1500 555 900 33 88]

Test case 13 [ArrayList]: subList method
list: [88 33 900 555 1500 1000]
sublist from 0 to 6: [88 33 900 555 1500 1000]
sublist from 1 to 3: [33 900]
sublist from 5 to 2: Index out of bounds in subList
sublist from 3 to 3: []

Test case 14 [ArrayList]: size and isEmpty methods
[].size() = 0
[].isEmpty() = true
[11 33 44 55 66 77 88].size() = 7
[11 33 44 55 66 77 88].isEmpty() = false
[5].size() = 1
[5].isEmpty() = false
[].size() = 0
[].isEmpty() = true

Test case 15 [ArrayList]: clear method
[11 33 44 55 66 77 88].clear() = []
size = 0, isEmpty = true
list after adding 1, addFirst(2), addLast(3): [2 1 3]
Unmodified original list: [11 33 44 55 66 77 88]

Test case 16 [ArrayList]: exceptions for invalid indices and empty lists
list: [11 33 44 55 66 77 88]
get(-1): ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException
get(7): ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException
set(7, 0): ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException
add(8, 0): ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException
remove(-1): ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException
Unmodified list: [11 33 44 55 66 77 88]
empty list: []
getFirst(): NoSuchElementException
getLast(): NoSuchElementException
removeFirst(): NoSuchElementException
iterator().next(): NoSuchElementException

Test case 17 [ArrayList]: equals method with different lists
[11 33 44 55 66 77 88].equals([11 33 44 55 66 77 88]) ? true
[11 33 44 55 66 77 88].equals([-1 33 44 55 66 77 88]) ? false
[11 33 44 55 66 77 88].equals([11 33 44 55 66 77]) ? false
[11 33 44 55 66 77 88].equals([88 77 66 55 44 33 11]) ? false
[11 33 44 55 66 77 88].equals("[11 33 44 55 66 77 88]") ? false
[].equals([]) ? true

Test case 18 [ArrayList]: methods with duplicate elements
list: [7 3 7 9 3 7]
[7 3 7 9 3 7].indexOf(7) = 0
[7 3 7 9 3 7].lastIndexOf(7) = 5
[7 3 7 9 3 7].indexOf(3) = 1
[7 3 7 9 3 7].lastIndexOf(3) = 4
[7 3 7 9 3 7].remove(7) = true -> [3 7 9 3 7]
[3 7 9 3 7].removeAll([7]) = [3 9 3]
[3 7 9 3 7].retainAll([3]) = [3 3]

Test case 19 [ArrayList]: sort method edge cases
empty list sorted: []
single element list sorted: [42]
already sorted list sorted: [11 33 44 55 66 77 88]
list sorted in reverse order: [88 77 66 55 44 33 11]
list with duplicates sorted: [3 3 7 7 9]

Test case 20 [ArrayList]: large number of elements
size after adding 150 elements: 150
getFirst() = -49, getLast() = 99, get(75) = 25
sum of elements: 3725
list after removing 140 elements: [90 91 92 93 94 95 96 97 98 99]


